{"id": "68:3b", "severity": "minor", "issues": [{"latin": "Veni in altitúdinem maris", "portuguese": "Cheguei ao alto-mar", "problem": "'alto-mar' is the idiom for the open sea, far from shore; 'altitudo maris' here is the deep of the sea, continuing the image of sinking (limo profundi, demersit). The idiom shifts the picture from depth to distance.", "fix": "Cheguei à profundeza do mar"}]},
{"id": "68:12", "severity": "minor", "issues": [{"latin": "factus sum illis in parábolam", "portuguese": "tornei-me para eles um termo de comparação", "problem": "'parabola' here is a proverb or byword, something people repeat in mockery; 'termo de comparação' is a neutral, almost technical phrase and loses the scorn.", "fix": "e tornei-me para eles um provérbio"}]},
{"id": "68:13", "severity": "minor", "issues": [{"latin": "in me psallébant", "portuguese": "contra mim cantavam", "problem": "'in me' with psallebant can be 'about me' or 'against me'; 'contra' settles it. 'de mim' would keep both readings open.", "fix": "e de mim cantavam os que bebiam vinho"}]},
{"id": "68:13b", "severity": "minor", "issues": [{"latin": "Ego vero oratiónem meam ad te, Dómine", "portuguese": "Eu, porém, dirijo-vos a minha oração, Senhor", "problem": "The Latin has no verb; supplying 'dirijo' is more than a copula and fixes a tense and a verb the Latin leaves out. It can be kept verbless in Portuguese.", "fix": "Eu, porém, a minha oração a vós, Senhor"}]},
{"id": "68:16", "severity": "minor", "issues": [{"latin": "tempéstas aquæ", "portuguese": "a tempestade das águas", "problem": "'aquæ' is singular; the plural is a change of number.", "fix": "Não me submerja a tempestade da água"}]},
{"id": "68:19", "severity": "minor", "issues": [{"latin": "éripe me", "portuguese": "libertai-me", "problem": "'eripe' means to snatch or tear out, and the same verb is 'arrancai-me' in 68:15; 'libertai' is weaker and blurs it with 'libera' (livrai), which appears in the same verse.", "fix": "por causa dos meus inimigos, arrancai-me"}]},
{"id": "68:22", "severity": "minor", "issues": [{"latin": "dedérunt in escam meam fel", "portuguese": "deram-me fel na minha comida", "problem": "'in escam' means 'as / for my food' (gall given as food), not gall put into the food; this parallels 'in siti mea ... aceto'.", "fix": "E deram-me fel por comida"}]}
], "overall": "A faithful translation of Ps 68 that follows the Latin throughout, keeping the Septuagint-based readings (substantia, altitudinem maris, reverentiam, vitulum novellum cornua producentem) without smoothing them toward the Hebrew. The pointing marks match the Latin in every verse. There are no critical or major faults, only minor points about sense, number and consistency: altitudo, parabola, in me, the verb supplied in 13b, aquæ, eripe and in escam."}
